faq:
  - question: Should I change my whole program when I start cutting?
    answer: >-
      Keep the same core lifts if you can. Familiar names make weekly
      comparisons possible. Cut junk volume before you cut the exercises that
      tell you whether strength is holding.
  - question: What if every session feels harder on a deficit?
    answer: >-
      Expect some sessions to feel worse. Judge the log: did you hit the
      planned sets? If loads stall for weeks, eat a bit more on training days
      or drop a set—not your entire plan.
  - question: Can cardio and lifting live in the same log on a cut?
    answer: >-
      Yes. One log for strength, walks, intervals, yoga, and rest days keeps
      the week honest so extra cardio does not sneak in unpaid.
